+
+## 14. Conversation list (opt-in)
+
+`transport.history` is the deployer's independent opt-in to exposing a user's conversation metadata to their client; enabling resume alone does not grant that disclosure. Retention remains the deployer's responsibility under #41. Opening a returned conversation requires `transport.resume` and the existing `?sessionId=` reconnect path.
+
+### Client frame: list_conversations
+
+| Field    | Type    | Required | Description                                                                                          |
+| -------- | ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `type`   | string  | Yes      | `"list_conversations"`                                                                               |
+| `limit`  | integer | No       | 1–200                                                                                                |
+| `before` | object  | No       | Both `updatedAt` (parseable date string) and `sessionId` (string), from the previous page's last row |
+
+The validator accepts this frame independently of feature configuration and diagnoses malformed limits and cursors by field name. ([validated by: validates history limits and composite cursors independently of configuration](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L128))
+
+### Server frame: conversation_list
+
+| Field           | Type   | Description                                                                                                        |
+| --------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| `type`          | string | `"conversation_list"`                                                                                              |
+| `conversations` | array  | Summary rows containing only `sessionId`, ISO-string `createdAt`, ISO-string `updatedAt`, and numeric `entryCount` |
+
+The server answers only on request, using the connection's authenticated user rather than any user id in the frame, and returns that user's metadata without conversation content or credentials, including the current conversation, in newest-first order with a composite cursor for paging and the existing resume path for opening a row. ([validated by: lists only the authenticated users metadata, pages ties and reopens a listed conversation](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L161))
+
+A disabled or unavailable list produces `UNSUPPORTED`, a store failure produces a sanitized `SERVER_ERROR` and a session-scoped log, and neither closes the connection or masquerades as an empty history. ([validated by: refuses unavailable history and sanitizes store failures without closing the socket](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L218))
+
+The list bypasses the per-session turn lock and has no `stream_end` of its own. ([validated by: answers history while a user turn holds the session lock](../../src/transport/conversationList.acceptance.test.ts#L278))
